   1992},
Abstract = {A horizontal Monochromatic Laser Transmission Path (MLTP) was used for
   monitoring of the transmission change in the urban boundary layer of the
   city of Leipzig. Measurements of the volume extinction coefficient
   employing this MLTP were carried out from March 1990 to March 1992. The
   influence of relative humidity on the extinction coefficient was
   considered. According to several weather conditions the relevant
   influence of the predominant air masses and the changing air pollution
   on the extinction coefficient should be investigated.},
