   Realities of the Contemporary World (PSIWORLD), Fac Psychol \& Educ Sci,
   Bucharest, ROMANIA, OCT 27-30, 2011},
Organization = {Romanian Soc Appl Expt Psychol},
Abstract = {The current study aimed to highlight the significant difference between
   the transduction results at / in two distinct moments: before and after
   applying a relaxation technique. The participants were 36 students from
   the Faculty of Psychology, aged between 19 and 37 years old (m=23;
   S.D.=5.18). The instrument: Aura Vision 5.1. By applying Wilcoxon
   signed-rank test the research hypotheses were confirmed (p<0.05). After
   the relaxation session, the participants were relaxed not only mentally
   but also physiologically. Hence, both the central and the sympathetic
   nervous system are activated, and the emotional energies can change into
   thermic, electric and electromagnetic energies. (C) 2012 Published by
   Elsevier B.V. Selection and/or peer-review under responsibility of
