   Management},
Abstract = {The western city groups of China have been faced many deep-rooted
   contradictions and problems that restrict the sustainable growth in the
   process of transforming from closed traditional agricultural districts
   to open tertiary industry cities and shifting from self-developing
   monomer cities to urban agglomerations with mutual support and communal
   development. In this context, this article will take the western city
   groups of China as the research object, sum up the problems in the
   process of sustainable development of the western city groups of China
   through literature research and survey research, and propose some
   appropriate countermeasures, such as the sustainable development of
   western city groups should be propelled under the guidance of uniform
   planning, focus on regional cooperation, rejuvenating traditional
   industrial bases, planning scientifically and properly, implementing the
   open urbanization strategy and accelerating the development of education
   in the western region, etc.},
