Abstract = {The research described in this article used a visual search task and
   demonstrated that the eye region alone can produce a threat superiority
   effect. Indeed, the magnitude of the threat superiority effect did not
   increase with whole-face, relative to eye-region-only, stimuli. The
   authors conclude that the configuration of the eyes provides a key
   signal of threat, which can mediate the search advantage for
   threat-related facial expressions.},
