   prevention application},
Booktitle = {2008 PROCEEDINGS OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SYSTEM
   SCIENCES: ITESS 2008, VOL 4},
Year = {2008},
Pages = {72-76},
Note = {International Conference on Informational Technology and Environmental
   System Science, Henan Polytechn Univ, Jiaozuo, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY
   15-17, 2008},
Abstract = {Forest fires cause significant economic damage and hazard to
   environment. Apart from preventive measures, early warning and fast
   extinction of fires are the only chance to avoid major casualties. and
   damage to nature. For the automatic detection and report of forest fires
   early, the clarity of object has more affection on accuracy of
   detection. When detecting a suspected fire, this system makes the camera
   zoom in the suspicious region, and executes auto-focusing to make the
   image clear in order to further automatically confirm the existences of
   the fire. This paper describes an auto-focusing system applying in
   forest fire-protection. It consists of a digital camera with a
   high-precision digital pan-and-tilt platform and an embedded control
   system. The embedded system can control pan-and-tilt platform and
   cameras which have optical zoom lens and focus set. In order to make the
   image clear, we compare with some well-known focus measures and propose
   a simple but efficient auto-focusing method based on spatial frequency
   domain. This method processes the center block of image based on
   discrete cosine transform (DCT).High-frequency energy is used to
   evaluate the clarity of image. Experimental results indicate that the
   method has high sensitivity and the entire system achieves the desired
   objective.},
