   Chartered Inst Bldg (CIOB); Council Sustainable Dev; Emerald; Hong Kong
   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc;
   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {In order to reasonably distribute resources and coordinate
   cross-boundary activities, regional planning still matters in Taiwan.
   However, the fact that regional planning system cannot work is often
   attributed to lack of superior legislation of territorial planning.
   Actually, what makes the regional planning system poorly perform is not
   the matter of territorial planning legislation but that of ignorance of
   Taiwan' specific local politics of planning. In our paper, we indicate
   the Achilles' heel of Taiwan's regional planning system behind the
   complex context of local political economy driven by developmental state
   and provide a brief review through the case of Northern Taiwan region to
   illustrate the institutional barrier to the new regional planning
   initiative under Taiwan' territorial restructuring. If we still ignore
   the weakness, what the new legislation can work will continue poorly
   behaving.},
