   Forest \& Range Expt Stn, SW Reg, Coronado Natl Forest},
Abstract = {While natural areas are generally perceived as desirable havens by city
   dwellers, the potential danger of fire is not always fully appreciated.
   People may correctly perceive the risk, but are unwilling to compromise
   their version of natural and aesthetically pleasing surroundings because
   environmental fears and desires are based largely on emotions rather
   than logic. Computer `'visualization'' technology may be more effective
   than words in motivating realistic response to fire danger in the
   wildland-urban interface.},
