   Univ; Siemens Ltd},
Abstract = {Cognitive neuroscience has provided powerful tools that now permit the
   investigation of human social cognition and behavior with unprecedented
   accuracy. This review summarizes some of the features of the human brain
   that differentiate it from the brains of other animals, some of the
   methods used in cognitive neuroscience, and concludes with an example of
   research from the author's own lab that implicates the amygdala in
   emotion recognition, social judgment, and autism.},
