   Management},
Abstract = {The rapid growth of electrolytic manganese metal (EMM) industries in
   China has made great contributions to the development of national
   industry and regional economy, and has also raised a number of alarming
   environmental and ecological problems. The critical reason is due to
   many factors: (1) raw material provided is not clean; (2) technological
   processes are not clean; (3) process control is not clean; and (4)
   environmental supervision and law enforcement is not strict. The EMM
   pollution prevention and control team of Chinese Research Academy of
   Environmental Sciences (CRAES) has successfully developed many
   technologies from the key processes of EMM pollution generated from EMM
   industries, including recovering manganese and chromium ion from
   wastewater, separating and recycling wastewater with manganese and
   chromium ion, extracting residual manganese from manganese residue and
   making harmless brick and so on. As well as accumulated a large number
   of theoretical basis and practical experience for studying EMM cleaner
   production (CP) technology. These processes can reduce environmental
   pollution, achieve resource-saving and environment-friendly production
   ideas, but they can also can improve the economic and social benefits of
   EMM industries.},
