   Bioscience (ICFEEB), Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 24-25, 2013},
Abstract = {The biochar derived from the pyrolysis of spent mushroom substrate (SMS)
   was investigated in this study. SMS biochars produced at different
   temperatures (400, 500, 600 and 700 degrees C) were characterized using
   a suite of analytical techniques. Detailed characterization indicated
   that the surface areas of biochars were increased with pyrolysis
   temperature. The SMS biochar consisted of high phosphorus (14.05\%),
   potassium (12.17\%), calcium (14.36\%) and magnesium (6.18\%). The
   properties provide a potential application for improving plant growth.},
