   (IC3E), Xiamen Univ Technol, Xiamen, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAR 01-03, 2018},
Organization = {Int Soc Environm Informat Sci; Asia Pacific Inst Sci \& Engn},
Abstract = {greenery system (VGS) applying in building design and construction is
   regarded as one of the solutions. Green Facade (GF), with the climber
   plants growing on the building facade, is one branch technology of VGS.
   This research is focused on the shading effect and the heat reflection
   performance of the GF in Hot humid Climate Area. A high-rise residential
   project with the GFs on east and south facade is chosen to measure and
   analyze. Results reveal that the air Ave. temperature (Temp) shading by
   the GFs in sunny days is reduced by 0.6 degrees C (E) and 0.7 degrees
   C(S), and the Max. reduction is up to 3.2 degrees C (E) and 3.8 degrees
   C(S). The surface Ave. Temp of GF is reduced 4.7 degrees C comparing to
   the bare wall, and the Ave. Temp of the whole facade is decreased about
   3-4 degrees C with GFs. This research has proved the effects of GFs and
   also show the GFs' potentials for energy reduction and urban heat
   environment improvement.},
