   Singapore, SINGAPORE, OCT, 2011},
Organization = {Singapore Inst Elect (SIE)},
Abstract = {In this paper, 16 economic, social and environmental indicators were
   used to evaluate the urban livability in Gansu. The principal component
   analysis revealed six principal components with eigenvalues more than 1,
   the most important of which represents economic development, and others
   represent environmental quality, geographical location, living
   standards, medical facilities, and urban traffic condition. The
   comprehensive scores of six principal components exhibited that the
   level of livability of the cities in Gansu is totally low, and the
   differences in livability between these cities are significant. The
   livability of cities in different regions are significant as well, with
   cities in Hexi corridor being more livable than those in eastern parts
   and northern cities being more livable than those in southern parts. (C)
   2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection and/or peer-review under
