Abstract = {Alexithymia is conceptualized as a disorder of emotion regulation
   mechanisms, which involves a dissociation of emotional and physic
   responses to life events and bodily sensations. Our results might
   suggest a possible relationship between the alexithymic construct and
   TNF levels in RA patients. These preliminary findings corroborate the
   integrated bidirectional interactions between neuropsychological
   mechanisms and the neuroendocrine-immune system in patients affected by
   autoimmune diseases and contribute to finding a common biological
   pathway linking alexithymia and autoimmune-inflammatory diseases.},
