Title = {Effect of Nec-1 in the Al-induced Loss of Nerve Cells in vitro
   and Its Relationship with the AD},
Booktitle = {8TH NATIONAL POSTGRADUATE SYMPOSIUM ON ENVIRONMENTAL AND OCCUPATIONAL
   MEDICINE, PROCEEDINGS},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {146-151},
Note = {8th National Postgraduate Conference on Environmental and Occupational
   Medicine, Suzhou, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 23-25, 2009},
Abstract = {Alzheimer's disease (AD) is a neurodegenerative disease of unknown
   reason. In recent years, its prevalence rate is getting higher and
   higher, and AD has age and gender differences. And its prevalence is
   expected to quadruple by the year 2047, so people are highly concerned
   about the prevention and treatment of the disease. Aluminum (Al) is
   considered the main cause of AD. AD patients generally have long-term
   exposure to high aluminum, and strong Aluminum intake capacity, but weak
   ability to excrete it. Human organs, especially the brain, is apt to be
   posioned by Al, but the distribution of aluminum in the brain in uneven,
   mainly concentrated in the cortex, hippocampus and striatum.
   Neurotoxicity of aluminum may be associated with neural cell apoptosis.
   Recently, Harvard Medical School Professor Junying Yuan and her research
   that they found new necrosis caused by a precise cell signaling pathway
   in the ``Nature Chemical Biology{''} in 2005, and named it necroptosis.
   The new findings caused great sensation in the academic community. Then,
   whether Nec-1 has effect on Al-induced loss of nerve cells? And whether
   it is useful to AD? We do research with the doubts above, through means
   of cell culture in vitro manufacturing Al injury model, and discuss
   Nec-1's role in cell protecting by different angles and methods. The
   results showed that Nec-1 can enhance cell viability after Al induced
   loss of nerve cells. And with the dose increasing,nerve cells even m any
   return to its normal levels, which indicate that Nec-1 has significant
   protective effect on nerve cells, which is consistent, with professional
   brothers. However, our results also indicated that Nec-1 not only can
   specificly and effectively inhibit procedural death of nerve cell but
   also have some effects to other cell death pathways such as autophagy,
   about which we are not very clear, may be it is indirectl. In all, a
   certain amount of Nec-1 can protect nerve cells from aluminum posioning,
   which is important and may provide new targets and ideas to the
   prevention and treatment of AD.},
