Abstract = {Catalepsy is a temporary state of immobility where the animals including
   man fail to correct the imposed posture It may be induced by primary
   emotions such as extreme fear, as well as by forced restraint on the
   movement and by drugs. Catalepsy tests were conducted by two methods,
   pinch method and incline-floor method. Learning related to the pinch
   method influences the adrenergic agonist-induced catalepsy duration in
   mice. Such learning effect could be mediated through thr
   amygdalo-hypothalamic pathways.},
