Year = {1999},
Volume = {3},
Pages = {289-294},
Note = {XIVth Annual International Occupational Ergonomics and Safety Conference
   1999, ORLANDO, FL, JUN 06-09, 1999},
Abstract = {In developing safely programs it is useful to examine what the
   perception of risk is:for various hazards. Risks may be accepted if the
   consequences are relatively mild. Most discussions of risk include two
   components: the likelihood of an event and the seriousness of its
   effects if it occurs. If the overall risk is considered unacceptable,
   the individual may use appropriate measures to avoid the hazard. If
   warnings emphasize the factors deemed important to the user they may be
   more effective. These studies evaluated relative contributions of
   probability of occurrence and probability of serious consequences on
   overall risk perceptions for a number of work and home type hazards.
   Although there was somewhat greater influence of consequences
   perception, the results were not conclusive, because the correlations of
   overall risk ratings with probability of occurrence and with probability
   of a serious consequence were affected by the order in which the ratings
   were made.},
